-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261103.1~sparky9~0 (2026-11-03)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The rebuild after an update is never capped (ORDER 361; Daniel, 2026-11-02: "Wheel-driver builds - or any build at update time - DO NEVER CAP EXECUTION"): it runs at normal priority on every processor; the transient service loses Nice=19, IOSchedulingClass=idle and CPUSchedulingPolicy=batch, the detached process its nice 19, the build its nice 10, and an automatic rebuild no longer leaves one processor out

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261102.2~sparky9~0 (2026-11-02)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * A failed update check that the problems engine kept and said no longer fails apt update; a failure nothing could keep still does
  * A repository without our FFmpeg source is said as such (check the source line) in the build, the update check and --status
  * An unreadable source index or invalid record has its own message in the build and --status, in nine languages
  * --status prints what it can before a source problem and then fails

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261102.1~sparky9~0 (2026-11-02)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Keep cleanup and build/update-check failures in sparky-stereo-problems; migrate legacy errors
  * Explain in nine languages which extra removals made the build tools stay
  * Check repository reads and background launch status; clear problems after success
  * Read --status and retry --cleanup through the shared engine; build message catalogs

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261102~sparky9~0 (2026-11-02)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Stop before package changes when an APT simulation fails or proposes removing existing packages
  * Report dependency cleanup failures, keep the affected package list and show the problem with --status
  * Preserve the original failure status when cleanup also fails; never report a failed cleanup as done
  * Add isolated failure checks and diagnostics in all nine languages


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261029~sparky9~0 (2026-10-29)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Added German, Japanese, Korean, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese strings

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261008.2~sparky9~0 (2026-10-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The build no longer stops at dh_shlibdeps on computers whose /etc/ld.so.conf.d lists another folder before the distribution's (CUDA's OpenCL, PipeWire's JACK): dpkg-shlibdeps now looks in the distribution's own library folders first, as on a clean build machine (found on the first host build, 2026-10-08)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261008.1~sparky9~0 (2026-10-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * First version: sparky-stereo-ffmpeg-fdk rebuilds the edition's FFmpeg (ffmpeg-dmo, build profile pkg.ffmpeg-dmo.fdk) on the user's own computer with Fraunhofer's AAC encoder
  * Says plainly before anything is built that the result is for that computer only (FFmpeg's LICENSE.md), and how long the build takes
  * Installs the result as VERSION+fdkN, kept by apt through a pin the build writes (the exact version of each installed package, with its architecture, at 1002); the 32-bit libraries are the edition's own, relabelled to the same version (Multi-Arch: same)
  * An apt hook rebuilds by itself, in the background, when the edition updates FFmpeg; --status, --remove (back to the edition's FFmpeg)
